# Clipper CLI

Clip long videos into vertical 9:16 shorts from the terminal. Zero
dependencies; talks to the same API the dashboard, the MCP server and the
webhooks use.

```bash
pip install clipper        # or: uvx clipper / pipx run clipper

export CLIPPER_API_KEY=osk_...   # from your account page at clipper.app

clipper process "https://youtube.com/watch?v=..." --wait
clipper clips <job_id>
clipper publish <job_id> 0 --platforms tiktok,youtube
clipper quota
```

Self-hosted instance? Point it at your own machine and skip the key:

```bash
export CLIPPER_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
clipper process "https://youtube.com/watch?v=..." --wait
```

For pipelines, prefer the webhook to `--wait`: pass `--webhook` and
`--webhook-secret` and Clipper POSTs once (HMAC-signed,
`X-Clipper-Signature: sha256=<hex>`) when the job ends, with clip titles
and durable download links.

The hosted free tier is 20 minutes/month with a watermark; paid plans from
$12/month. The self-hosted edition is MIT and has no meter. Agent-native
version of the same surface: [clipper.app/mcp](https://www.clipper.app/mcp).
